/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# OMC operational state. Kept out of the repo by convention; note that this
# means `.omc/plans/shepherd-consensus-plan.md` is NOT present in a CI checkout,
# which is why `cargo xtask claim-ledger` is a local gate command and not a CI
# step. `cargo xtask gate --audit` reads `xtask/ac-map.toml`, which IS committed,
# so it does run in CI.
/.omc/
/.remember/

# Phase 0b/0c artifacts that are generated, large, or machine-specific.
/fixtures/
# `bench-baseline.json` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is the §9 Phase 0a/0b
# gate's evidence artifact, and a gate whose evidence exists only on the machine
# that produced it cannot be audited afterwards — which is exactly what someone
# re-deriving the index decision in six months would need. It is tens of KiB of
# summary statistics, not bulk data: per-candidate p50/p95/p99, RSS, on-disk
# size, warm-vs-cold, per-class hit counts, and the probed reference machine.
# Per-query latency samples are reduced to percentiles in-process and never
# written, so there is no large raw trace to keep out.
